      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "step-1-1",
          "step": "1.1",
          "claim": "[Orthogonality] Let $m,n\\in\\mathbb N$ with $n\\ge1$. By [F2] with $\\varphi=ag_n$ and $\\psi=g_m$, $\\langle a^\\dagger ag_n,g_m\\rangle=\\langle ag_n,ag_m\\rangle$; by [F2] with $\\varphi=g_n$ and $\\psi=ag_m$, $\\langle g_n,a^\\dagger ag_m\\rangle=\\langle ag_n,ag_m\\rangle$ as well. Using $a^\\dagger ag_k=kg_k$ from [F1] on both sides, $n\\langle g_n,g_m\\rangle=m\\langle g_n,g_m\\rangle$. If $n=m$ this gives no information; if $n\\ne m$ and $n,m\\ge1$ it gives $\\langle g_n,g_m\\rangle=0$. If $m=0$ use $ag_0=0$: then $\\langle ag_n,ag_0\\rangle=0$, and the first identity reads $n\\langle g_n,g_0\\rangle=0$, so $\\langle g_n,g_0\\rangle=0$ for $n\\ge1$.",
          "inputs": [
            "F1",
            "F2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "step-1-2",
          "step": "1.2",
          "claim": "[Eigenvalue equation] By [F4], $Y^2-\\partial_y^2=2a^\\dagger a+I$ on $P$. Evaluating at $g_n$ and using [F1] gives $(-\\partial_y^2+Y^2)g_n=2ng_n+g_n=(2n+1)g_n$ as classes in $L^2$; the left side is computed on the smooth representative $g_n$, and the equality of classes holds because the two sides are continuous functions agreeing in $L^2$. The displayed form for $\\varphi\\in P$ with $Y^2\\varphi=y^2\\varphi$ is the same identity.",
          "inputs": [
            "F1",
            "F4"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "step-2-1",
          "step": "2.1",
          "claim": "[Unit norms] $\\|g_0\\|=1$ by [F1]. For $n\\ge0$, applying [F2] with $\\varphi=g_n$, $\\psi=a^\\dagger g_n$ gives $\\|a^\\dagger g_n\\|^2=\\langle a^\\dagger g_n,a^\\dagger g_n\\rangle=\\langle g_n,aa^\\dagger g_n\\rangle=(n+1)\\|g_n\\|^2$ by $aa^\\dagger g_n=(n+1)g_n$ from [F1]. Since $g_{n+1}=a^\\dagger g_n/\\sqrt{n+1}$ by [F1], $\\|g_{n+1}\\|^2=\\|a^\\dagger g_n\\|^2/(n+1)=\\|g_n\\|^2$. Induction gives $\\|g_n\\|=1$ for every $n$. Together with step 1.1, $\\langle g_n,g_m\\rangle=\\delta_{nm}$.",
          "inputs": [
            "1.1",
            "F1",
            "F2",
            "F3"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "step-3-1",
          "step": "3.1",
          "claim": "[Ladder pairings] For $n\\ne m$, $\\langle ag_n,ag_m\\rangle=\\sqrt{nm}\\langle g_{n-1},g_{m-1}\\rangle=0$ by step 2.1 when $n,m\\ge1$, and $\\langle ag_0,\\cdot\\rangle=0$; for $n=m$ it equals $n\\|g_{n-1}\\|^2=n$. Likewise $\\langle a^\\dagger g_n,a^\\dagger g_m\\rangle=\\sqrt{(n+1)(m+1)}\\langle g_{n+1},g_{m+1}\\rangle=(n+1)\\delta_{nm}$.",
          "inputs": [
            "2.1",
            "F1"
          ]
