          "source": "def-test-function-space-d-of-an-open-set",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Let $\\Omega\\subseteq\\mathbb R^n$ be open, with $n\\ge1$. A complex-valued function is smooth if its real and imaginary parts are $C^k$ for every finite $k$, in the sense of [[def-ck-and-multi-index-notation-in-several-variables]]. Coordinate derivatives act on these two parts separately. We write $\\partial^\\alpha$ for the multi-index convention there, and $\\partial^0\\varphi=\\varphi$.\n\nThe **test-fu",
