      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "step-1-1",
          "step": "1.1",
          "claim": "[Well-definedness and densities] For $x\\in D(a)$ the coefficients $\\sqrt{m+1}c_{m+1}$ are square summable with $\\sum_m(m+1)|c_{m+1}|^2=\\sum_{n\\ge1}n|c_n|^2<\\infty$, so the series $ax=\\sum_m\\sqrt{m+1}c_{m+1}e_m$ converges in $H$ and $\\|ax\\|^2=\\sum_{n\\ge1}n|c_n|^2$ by [F1]; the same computation gives the formulas for $a^\\dagger x$ and $Nx$. Linearity is coefficientwise. Every finite combination of the $e_n$ lies in all three domains, and $D_0$ is dense in $H$ by [F1], so the three domains are dense.",
          "inputs": [
            "F1",
            "F3"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "step-1-2",
          "step": "1.2",
          "claim": "[$a^*=a^\\dagger$] First let $y\\in D(a^*)$ and $w:=a^*y$. Testing the defining identity $\\langle ax,y\\rangle=\\langle x,w\\rangle$ on $x=e_m$ ($m\\ge1$) gives $\\sqrt m\\,\\overline{\\langle y,e_{m-1}\\rangle}=\\overline{\\langle w,e_m\\rangle}$, that is $\\sqrt m\\langle y,e_{m-1}\\rangle=\\langle w,e_m\\rangle$; hence $\\sum_{m\\ge1}m|\\langle y,e_{m-1}\\rangle|^2=\\sum_{m\\ge1}|\\langle w,e_m\\rangle|^2\\le\\|w\\|^2<\\infty$, so $y\\in D(a^\\dagger)$ and $a^\\dagger y=\\sum_{m\\ge1}\\sqrt m\\langle y,e_{m-1}\\rangle e_m=\\sum_{m\\ge1}\\langle w,e_m\\rangle e_m=w$ by [F1]. Thus $a^*\\subseteq a^\\dagger$. Conversely let $y\\in D(a^\\dagger)$ and $x\\in D(a)$; then $\\langle ax,y\\rangle=\\sum_{m\\ge0}\\sqrt{m+1}c_{m+1}\\overline{d_m}$ with $d_m=\\langle y,e_m\\rangle$, absolutely convergent by [F3] since $\\sum_m(m+1)|c_{m+1}|^2=\\|ax\\|^2<\\infty$ and $\\sum_m|d_m|^2=\\|y\\|^2$, and the same series equals $\\sum_{n\\ge1}c_n\\overline{\\sqrt n\\,d_{n-1}}=\\langle x,a^\\dagger y\\rangle$; hence the functional $x\\mapsto\\langle ax,y\\rangle$ is bounded on $(D(a),\\|\\cdot\\|)$ by $\\|y\\|$, so $y\\in D(a^*)$ and $a^*y=a^\\dagger y$. Therefore $a^*=a^\\dagger$.",
          "inputs": [
            "F1",
            "F2",
            "F3"
          ]
        },
