        },
        {
          "fact": "F4",
          "source": "thm-geometric-series",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $r \\in \\mathbb{R}$ and let $r^k$ be the integer power ([[def-integer-power]]),\nso that $r^0 = 1$ for every $r$, including $r = 0$.\n\n1. If $|r| < 1$ then the series $\\sum r^k$ converges ([[def-series]]) and\n   $$\\sum_{k=0}^{\\infty} r^{k} \\;=\\; \\frac{1}{1-r} .$$\n2. If $|r| \\ge 1$ then $\\sum r^k$ diverges.",
          "uses": [
            "2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F5",
          "source": "thm-nrqm-oscillator-hermite-recurrence",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice ([[def-countable-choice]]). Let $L^2=L^2(\\mathbb R,dy)$ be the complex Lebesgue space with inner product $\\langle\\varphi,\\psi\\rangle=\\int_{\\mathbb R}\\varphi(y)\\overline{\\psi(y)}\\,dy$ linear in the first argument ([[def-l-p-space-as-a-quotient-by-null-functions]], [[def-complex-lp-and-euclidean-test-function-conventions]]). Write $g_0$ for the function $g_0(y):=",
          "uses": [
            "2.2"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "step-1-1",
          "step": "1.1",
          "claim": "[Convergence and normalization] For $N\\ge M$, the partial sums $S_N:=e^{-|z|^2/2}\\sum_{n\\le N}\\frac{z^n}{\\sqrt{n!}}g_n$ satisfy $\\|S_N-S_M\\|^2=e^{-|z|^2}\\sum_{M<n\\le N}\\frac{|z|^{2n}}{n!}$ by [F1]. As $N,M\\to\\infty$ the right side tends to $0$ because $\\sum_n\\frac{|z|^{2n}}{n!}=e^{|z|^2}<\\infty$ by [F3]; hence $(S_N)$ is Cauchy and $\\psi_z:=\\lim_NS_N\\in L^2$ exists, and taking limits in the same identity gives $\\|\\psi_z\\|^2=e^{-|z|^2}\\sum_n\\frac{|z|^{2n}}{n!}=1$. Uniqueness of the coefficient sequence is orthonormality [F1].",
          "inputs": [
            "F1",
            "F3"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "step-2-1",
          "step": "2.1",
          "claim": "[Number domains] Fix $k\\in\\mathbb N$ and let $a_n:=n^{2k}|z|^{2n}/n!\\ge0$. For $n\\ge1$, $\\frac{a_{n+1}}{a_n}=(\\frac{n+1}{n})^{2k}\\frac{|z|^2}{n+1}\\to0$, so there is $N$ with $a_{n+1}\\le\\frac12a_n$ for $n\\ge N$; by [F4], $\\sum_{n\\ge N}a_n\\le2a_N<\\infty$, and the finitely many initial terms are finite. Hence $\\sum_nn^{2k}|c_n|^2=e^{-|z|^2}\\sum_na_n<\\infty$. Since $D(N^k)=\\{x:\\sum_nn^{2k}|\\langle x,g_n\\rangle|^2<\\infty\\}$ (inducting the domain formula of [[lem-nrqm-oscillator-closed-ladder-domains]](a) for $N$), this says $\\psi_z\\in D(N^k)$.",
          "inputs": [
            "1.1",
            "F1",
            "F4"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "step-2-2",
          "step": "2.2",
          "claim": "[$a\\psi_z=z\\psi_z$] Each partial sum $S_N$ is a finite combination of the $g_n$, so $S_N\\in D(N)\\subseteq D(a)$; by [F5], $aS_N=e^{-|z|^2/2}\\sum_{n=1}^Nz^n\\sqrt n\\,g_{n-1}/\\sqrt{n!}=ze^{-|z|^2/2}\\sum_{m=0}^{N-1}\\frac{z^m}{\\sqrt{m!}}g_m=zS_{N-1}$. As $N\\to\\infty$, $S_N\\to\\psi_z$ and $aS_N\\to z\\psi_z$ by step 1.1; since $a$ is closed [F2], $\\psi_z\\in D(a)$ and $a\\psi_z=z\\psi_z$. Taking norms, $\\|a\\psi_z\\|=|z|$ by (a).",
          "inputs": [
            "1.1",
            "F2",
            "F5"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "step-2-3",
          "step": "2.3",
          "claim": "[Inner products] For $z,w\\in\\mathbb C$, $\\langle\\psi_z,\\psi_w\\rangle=e^{-(|z|^2+|w|^2)/2}\\sum_n\\frac{z^n\\overline w^{\\,n}}{n!}$ by [F1] applied to the two convergent series, and $\\sum_n\\frac{(z\\overline w)^n}{n!}=e^{z\\overline w}$ by [F3] applied to the series of the complex number $z\\overline w$; hence $\\langle\\psi_z,\\psi_w\\rangle=e^{-(|z|^2+|w|^2)/2+z\\overline w}=e^{-|z-w|^2/2}$, which is real and positive. Then $\\|\\psi_z-\\psi_w\\|^2=\\|\\psi_z\\|^2+\\|\\psi_w\\|^2-2\\operatorname{Re}\\langle\\psi_z,\\psi_w\\rangle=2(1-e^{-|z-w|^2/2})$, which vanishes exactly when $z=w$; the map is injective.",
          "inputs": [
            "1.1",
            "F1",
            "F3"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "step-3-1",
          "step": "3.1",
          "claim": "[Number and creation moments] By step 2.1 with $k=1$, $\\psi_z\\in D(N)$ and $N\\psi_z$ has coefficients $nc_n$; hence $\\langle N\\psi_z,\\psi_z\\rangle=\\sum_nn|c_n|^2=e^{-|z|^2}\\sum_n\\frac{n|z|^{2n}}{n!}$. The series reindexes as $|z|^2\\sum_{m\\ge0}\\frac{|z|^{2m}}{m!}=|z|^2e^{|z|^2}$ by [F3], so the value is $|z|^2$. Next, $\\|a^\\dagger\\psi_z\\|^2=\\langle a^\\dagger\\psi_z,a^\\dagger\\psi_z\\rangle=\\langle\\psi_z,aa^\\dagger\\psi_z\\rangle=\\langle\\psi_z,(N+I)\\psi_z\\rangle=|z|^2+1$ using [F2] and $\\psi_z\\in D(N)$. Finally $\\psi_0=g_0$ since all coefficients with $n\\ge1$ vanish and $\\|\\psi_0\\|=1$.",
          "inputs": [
            "1.1",
            "2.1",
            "F1",
            "F2",
            "F3"
          ]
        }
      ],
