          "claim": "[(a) Hamiltonian as a number operator] Let $f\\in D(H_{\\mathrm{osc}})$ with $c_n=\\langle f,\\psi_n\\rangle$; by [F1] this means $\\sum_n(n+\\frac12)^2|c_n|^2<\\infty$, which is equivalent to $\\sum_nn^2|c_n|^2<\\infty$ because $n^2\\le4(n+\\frac12)^2$ and $(n+\\frac12)^2\\le2n^2+\\frac12$ for all $n\\ge0$; hence $D(H_{\\mathrm{osc}})=D(N_\\psi)$ by [F1] and the transported domain formula, and $H_{\\mathrm{osc}}f=\\sum_n\\hbar\\omega(n+\\frac12)c_n\\psi_n=\\hbar\\omega\\bigl(\\sum_nnc_n\\psi_n+\\frac12f\\bigr)=\\hbar\\omega(N_\\psi f+\\frac12f)$.",
          "inputs": [
