          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice ([[def-countable-choice]]). Let $L^2=L^2(\\mathbb R,dy)$ be the complex Lebesgue space with inner product linear in the first argument, and let $g_0,P,(g_n)_{n\\in\\mathbb N}$ and $H_n$ be as in [[thm-nrqm-oscillator-hermite-recurrence]]. Define $h:=fg_0\\in L^1(\\mathbb R)$ for $f\\in L^2$ and write $\\widehat h(\\xi)=\\int_{\\mathbb R}h(y)e^{-2\\pi i\\xi y}\\,dy$ for its ",
