          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice ([[def-countable-choice]]). Let $L^2=L^2(\\mathbb R,dy)$ be the complex Lebesgue space with inner product linear in the first argument, and let $g_0,P,a,a^\\dagger,g_n$ and $H_n$ be as in [[thm-nrqm-oscillator-hermite-recurrence]]. Then, for all $m,n\\in\\mathbb N$:\n\n(a) $\\langle g_n,g_m\\rangle=\\delta_{nm}$; in particular $(g_n)_{n\\in\\mathbb N}$ is an orthonormal f",
