          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice ([[def-countable-choice]]), let $a,b\\ge1$ and identify $\\mathbb R^{a+b}=\\mathbb R^a\\times\\mathbb R^b$ with Lebesgue measure ([[def-l-p-space-as-a-quotient-by-null-functions]]); write $H_a=L^2(\\mathbb R^a)$, $H_b=L^2(\\mathbb R^b)$. Then there is a unique linear isometry\n\n$$\\Theta:H_a\\widehat\\otimes H_b\\longrightarrow L^2(\\mathbb R^{a+b})$$\n\nwith $\\Theta(f\\otimes",
          "uses": [
            "1.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F3",
          "source": "lem-nrqm-oscillator-diagonal-adjoint-and-graph-core-lemma",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice ([[def-countable-choice]]). Let $H$ be a complex Hilbert space ([[def-hilbert-space]]) with inner product linear in the first argument, let $(e_n)_{n\\in\\mathbb N}$, where $\\mathbb N=\\{0,1,2,\\dots\\}$, be a complete orthonormal family of $H$ ([[def-orthonormal-family-complete-orthonormal-system-and-hilbert-basis]]), and let $(\\lambda_n)_{n\\in\\mathbb N}\\subseteq\\m",
          "uses": [
