          "fact": "F3",
          "source": "thm-chain-rule",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $A, B \\subseteq \\mathbb{R}$, let $g : A \\to \\mathbb{R}$ with\n$g[A] \\subseteq B$ and let $f : B \\to \\mathbb{R}$, so that the composite\n$f \\circ g : A \\to \\mathbb{R}$ is defined. Let $c \\in A$ be a limit point of\n$A$ ([[def-limit-point-r]]) at which $g$ is differentiable\n([[def-derivative]]), put $b := g(c)$, and suppose $b$ is a limit point of $B$\nat which $f$ is differentiable. Then $f \\circ g",
          "uses": [
            "2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F3",
          "source": "thm-derivative-of-exponential",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "The real exponential function is $C^\\infty$, and for every $m\\in\\mathbb N$,\n$$\\exp^{(m)}=\\exp.$$\nIn particular $(\\exp)'=\\exp$.",
          "uses": [
            "2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F3",
          "source": "def-complex-exponential",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Let $\\iota_{\\mathbb R}\\colon\\mathbb N\\to\\mathbb R$ be the canonical-natural map\nof [[def-canonical-natural]], and let $j\\colon\\mathbb R\\to\\mathbb C$ be the real\nembedding $j(x)=x+i0$ from [[def-complex-numbers-and-arithmetic]]. For every\n$n\\in\\mathbb N$, the factorial $n!$ is nonzero by\n[[def-factorial-and-falling-factorial]], so\n$\\iota_{\\mathbb R}(n!)>0$ by [[lem-of-naturals-positive]] and conseq",
          "uses": [
            "2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F4",
          "source": "thm-nrqm-oscillator-oscillator-scaling-and-exact-realization",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice ([[def-countable-choice]]). Fix real parameters $m>0$, $\\omega>0$, $\\hbar>0$, put $\\ell:=\\sqrt{\\hbar/(m\\omega)}>0$, and let $g_0,P,(g_n)_{n\\in\\mathbb N}$ be the Hermite data of [[thm-nrqm-oscillator-hermite-recurrence]] in $L^2(\\mathbb R,dy)$, so that $(g_n)$ is a complete orthonormal family by [[thm-nrqm-oscillator-hermite-completeness]]. Define\n\n$$D:L^2(\\math",
          "uses": [
            "2.1"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "step-1-1",
          "step": "1.1",
          "claim": "[(a) levels] By [F1], each $\\psi_n$ is a unit eigenvector with eigenvalue $\\hbar\\omega(n+\\frac12)$, and $\\sigma(H_{\\mathrm{osc}})$ is exactly the set of these numbers. Hence $E_0=\\hbar\\omega/2$, so $E_0/(\\hbar\\omega)=\\frac12$, and $E_{n+1}-E_n=\\hbar\\omega$ for every $n$, so $(E_{n+1}-E_n)/(\\hbar\\omega)=1$.",
          "inputs": [
            "F1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "step-1-2",
          "step": "1.2",
          "claim": "[(c) $d$-dimensional ground energy] In the isotropic $d$-dimensional operator $H$ of [[thm-nrqm-oscillator-multidimensional-oscillator-completeness]]$\\,$(d), the eigenvalues are $\\hbar\\omega(M+\\frac d2)$, $M\\in\\mathbb N$, so the smallest is $\\hbar\\omega\\cdot\\frac d2$: the ground energy is $\\frac d2\\hbar\\omega$, equal to $\\frac32\\hbar\\omega$ for $d=3$, and the increment of $M$ by one raises the energy by $\\hbar\\omega$.",
          "inputs": [
            "F1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "step-2-1",
          "step": "2.1",
          "claim": "[(b) ground eigenfunction] By [F2], $\\psi_0(x)=\\ell^{-1/2}\\pi^{-1/4}e^{-x^2/(2\\ell^2)}$. Using [F3], $-\\frac{\\hbar^2}{2m}\\psi_0''+\\frac{m\\omega^2}{2}x^2\\psi_0=\\bigl[\\frac{\\hbar^2}{2m\\ell^2}+\\bigl(-\\frac{\\hbar^2}{2m\\ell^4}+\\frac{m\\omega^2}{2}\\bigr)x^2\\bigr]\\psi_0$, and by [F4] the coefficient of $x^2$ vanishes while the constant term is $\\frac{\\hbar\\omega}{2}$; hence $H_{\\mathrm{osc}}\\psi_0=\\frac{\\hbar\\omega}{2}\\psi_0$ pointwise, in agreement with $H_{\\mathrm{osc}}\\psi_0=\\hbar\\omega(0+\\frac12)\\psi_0$ from [F1].",
          "inputs": [
            "1.1",
            "F1",
            "F2",
            "F3",
            "F4"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "step-3-1",
          "step": "3.1",
          "claim": "[(d) minimality] By [F1] the spectrum is the closed discrete set $\\{\\hbar\\omega(n+\\frac12):n\\in\\mathbb N\\}$, whose infimum is its least element $\\hbar\\omega/2=E_0$; no smaller value belongs to the spectrum.",
          "inputs": [
            "1.1",
            "F1"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "routine_steps": [],
