          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "step-1-3",
          "step": "1.3",
          "claim": "[(c) variance] Expanding $(N-|z|^2I)^2=N^2-2|z|^2N+|z|^4I$ and using [F3], $\\sum_n(n-|z|^2)^2p_n=e^{-|z|^2}\\sum_n(n^2-2|z|^2n+|z|^4)\\frac{|z|^{2n}}{n!}$. With $t=|z|^2$, the three series are $\\sum_nn^2\\frac{t^n}{n!}=(t^2+t)e^t$, $\\sum_nn\\frac{t^n}{n!}=te^t$ and $\\sum_n\\frac{t^n}{n!}=e^t$, obtained from the absolutely convergent exponential series by reindexing ($\\sum_{n\\ge1}\\frac{n\\,t^n}{n!}=t\\sum_{m\\ge0}\\frac{t^m}{m!}$ and $\\sum_{n\\ge2}\\frac{n(n-1)t^n}{n!}=t^2\\sum_{m\\ge0}\\frac{t^m}{m!}$); multiplying by $e^{-t}$ gives $(t^2+t)-2t^2+t^2=t=|z|^2$.",
          "inputs": [
