          "claim": "[(d) Poisson form] By (a)-(c) the distribution has total mass $1$, mean $|z|^2=\\lambda$ and variance $|z|^2=\\lambda$, and its weights are $e^{-\\lambda}\\lambda^n/n!$, which is the Poisson distribution with parameter $\\lambda$; if $z\\ne0$ then $\\lambda>0$ and $p_n>0$ for every $n$, so no outcome is excluded.",
          "inputs": [
            "1.1",
